>>
Rule 1 (input tensor must be 4-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 4
>>
Rule 2 (data format must be either 'channels_last' or 'channels_first')
{v_1 : str} |= v_1 = "channels_last" ∨ v_1 = "channels_first"
>>
Rule 3 (cropping parameter must be non-negative)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (input spatial dimensions must be greater than twice the cropping size when cropping is an integer)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_2 = "channels_last" then shape(v_3, 1) > 2 * v_1 ∧ shape(v_3, 2) > 2 * v_1 else shape(v_3, 2) > 2 * v_1 ∧ shape(v_3, 3) > 2 * v_1
>>
Rule 5 (cropping tuple must have exactly 2 elements and all elements must be non-negative)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ v_1[0] ≥ 0 ∧ v_1[1] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 6 (input tensor should have float or integer data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
>>
Rule 7 (input spatial dimensions must be greater than twice the cropping tuple values when cropping is a tuple of 2 integers)
{v_1 : tuple(int), v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ (if v_2 = "channels_last" then shape(v_3, 1) > 2 * v_1[0] ∧ shape(v_3, 2) > 2 * v_1[1] else shape(v_3, 2) > 2 * v_1[0] ∧ shape(v_3, 3) > 2 * v_1[1])
>>
Rule 12 (cropping list of ints must have length 2 and non-negative values)
{v_1 : list(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 13 (cropping tuple of ints must have length 2 and non-negative values)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 14 (input tensor should have a numeric data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8
